{title:'A safe way back',nav:'Undo & recovery',description:'Undo a published mistake while keeping the shared history intact.',duration:3,steps:[['Inspect the latest change','git show HEAD','git show HEAD'],['Undo with a new commit','git revert HEAD','git revert HEAD'],['Share the correction','git push origin main','git push origin main']],insight:['Undo without erasing','Revert adds an inverse commit. Reset moves a branch pointer; --hard can discard local work. Prefer revert for shared commits.'],hint:'A revert preserves the original commit and records a correction.'}
